{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nOnce Jira returns a key, local persistence can still fail. The canonical label is the durable remote identity floor; the entity property is optional enrichment. Local confirmation must use RP-02 as the single identity owner.\n\n## Outcome\nAfter create returns a key, FIRST persist the known key on the still-pending RP-02 entry (`record_pending_key` + `save`) so a crash in the create->label window is deterministically recoverable via the keyed-pending branch; THEN attach the canonical `rebar-id:<local_id>` label, attempt the optional property, and LAST confirm the binding (`bind_confirm` + save). Any failure after create returns a typed known-key safety abort that retains the keyed-pending binding and never deletes the remote issue.\n\n## Plan\n1. Require the RP-02 repository/lifecycle/recovery facade to be available; do not create a second binding writer.\n2. Persist the known key on the STILL-PENDING entry FIRST — `record_pending_key(local_id, jira_key)` (plus the immutable numeric id when the store supports it) then `save()` — BEFORE attaching the canonical label. This matches the story-9622 write-ahead protocol so a create->label-window crash recovers deterministically via the keyed-pending branch with no Jira search; a persist failure here rolls back and aborts before any label write.\n3. Then attach the canonical `rebar-id:<local_id>` label, and attempt the optional entity property second. Treat a property unsupported/permission failure as a visible enrichment failure that cannot erase the label floor.\n4. Confirm the binding LAST — `bind_confirm(local_id, jira_key)` through its unit of work — so local confirmation follows the label (per AC), while the durable key was already recorded before the label.\n5. If label, property, or persistence fails after create, preserve the known key, the keyed-pending/recovery evidence, the remote issue (NO delete — bug 387d), and the exact terminal disposition.\n6. Execute later lifecycle intents only after their remote postcondition is proven.\n\n## Testing\nFault cuts after returned key, before/during known-key save, during label, during property, and during confirmation assert remote containment (issue never deleted), local bytes (keyed-pending recorded before label), and exact typed known-key outcomes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The known key is recorded on the still-pending binding (`record_pending_key` + `save`) BEFORE the canonical label; the canonical label is attempted before the optional property and before local confirmation (`bind_confirm`).\n- [ ] Unsupported or forbidden property remains visible and cannot remove a successful label.\n- [ ] Known key and confirmation persist only through the RP-02 `BindingStore` facade.\n- [ ] Every post-create failure reports the known key and retains recovery evidence.\n- [ ] No post-create failure deletes the remote issue.\n- [ ] Other lifecycle intents execute only after their remote postconditions are proven.\n\n## Out of scope\nWhole-pass crash/restart convergence, dependency release, and production create cutover."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787699941861738001,"uuid":"d3ae0408-5e86-4d64-bf3c-5c8cf81d554b"}